<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spillings Hoard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 870</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spillings Hoard is the largest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> hoard ever found, discovered on a farm at Spillings in northern Gotland in 1999. Buried around 870, it contains about 67 kilograms of silver, including more than 14,000 coins, mostly Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dirham">dirhams</a>, with arm rings and ingots, as well as some 20 kilograms of bronze. It is displayed at the Gotland Museum in Visby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spillings-hoard.jpg" alt="Spillings Hoard" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: W.carter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spillings_Silver_Hoard_2_closeup.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
